            <div xml:id="d967-a1">

                <pb facs="0936" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg838"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Osma to Mr.
                            Neill</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-11-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 37.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé</hi>: I have the pleasure to inform your
                    honor that the national Congress, by virtue of its attributes, has approved the
                    amendment introduced by the Senate of the United States of America in the treaty
                    of extradition that was signed on November 28, 1899, by his excellency, Mr.
                    Dudley, and the chief of this chancellery at that time.</p>
                <p>The ratification documents are now ready for exchange.</p>
                <p>I reiterate, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Felipe de Osma.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
